given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bruil</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Power</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Duer</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Auquier</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Cloetta</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Czemy</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Mazur</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Czimbalmos</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Tountas</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Hagquist</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kilroe</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><collab>the KIDSCREEN Group</collab></person-group><article-title>The KIDSCREEN quality of life measure for children and adolsecents: psychometric results from a cross-cultural survey in 13 European countries</article-title><source>Value Health</source><comment></comment></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Eurostat yearbook '96</collab></person-group><source>A statistical view on Europe 1985&#x02013;1995</source><year>1996</year><publisher-name>Luxembourg: Eurostat</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>European Commission</collab></person-group><article-title>Eurostat</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://europa.eu.int/comm/eurostat/"/><comment>[cited 2007 May 5]</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>EOS Gallup Europe</collab></person-group><article-title>The situation of telecommunications services in the regions of the European Union</article-title><source>Residential survey</source><year>1999</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http:/